# Settings for backup/backup.sh on the production host (#300). Copy to
# backup/backup.env, which is gitignored. The local settings have defaults;
# the three off-site settings at the end do not, and a run without
# --local-only fails until all three are set.

# Where the local dumps and last-success go. Outside Desktop, Documents and
# Downloads: macOS guards those per app, and a launchd job cannot answer the
# permission prompt.
# BACKUP_DIR=$HOME/Backups/planning-hub

# How many dumps to keep, newest by name. 90 nightly runs are about three
# months, at tens of KB each.
# BACKUP_KEEP=90

# The off-site copy (docs/backup.md, "Install the off-site copy").
#
# The age recipient: the public key, which can encrypt but not decrypt. The
# identity that matches it lives on the maintainer's MacBook and in the
# password manager, never on this host.
# BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT=age1...
#
# The backup user on the VPS. Its host key must already be in known_hosts:
# BatchMode refuses an unknown one.
# BACKUP_REMOTE=planninghub-backup@<vps>
#
# The private key whose public half is pinned to the receiver there.
# BACKUP_SSH_KEY=$HOME/.ssh/planninghub_backup_ed25519
